{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (via the cobbler-scaffold orchestrator) issued stitch task #5300 to implement srd029-comm R4.1-R4.4 requirements for the `cmd/comm` utility. These requirements cover exit codes and SIGPIPE handling:\n   - R4.1: Exit 0 on successful processing with no order violations\n   - R4.2: Exit 1 when input file cannot be opened, print error to stderr\n   - R4.3: Exit 1 when a write error occurs on stdout\n   - R4.4: Handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) via pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler\n   \n   Files to modify: `cmd/comm/main.go` and `cmd/comm/comm_test.go`. Must follow existing patterns, use differential testing against `gcomm`, set LC_ALL=C. No git commands allowed.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern using `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests`\n   - SIGPIPE handling via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - GNU comm reference binary (`gcomm`) from Homebrew coreutils\n   - Exit code behavior matching GNU coreutils\n   - stderr normalization for program name differences (gcomm vs comm)\n   - LC_ALL=C for byte-for-byte comparison\n   - Buffered I/O with `bufio.Writer` and flush error handling\n   - EPIPE detection via `errors.Is(err, syscall.EPIPE)`\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd029-comm.yaml`\n     - Contains the full SRD specification for comm. R4 section (lines 54-64) defines exit codes and SIGPIPE requirements.\n     - R4.1: exit 0 on success, R4.2: exit 1 on file open error with stderr message, R4.3: exit 1 on stdout write error, R4.4: SIGPIPE via InstallSIGPIPEHandler\n\n   - `cmd/comm/main.go` (263 lines, existing implementation)\n     - Already implements R4.1-R4.4 in existing code:\n     - R4.4: `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at line 27\n     - R4.1: `compare()` returns 0 on success at line 186\n     - R4.2: `run()` prints error to stderr and returns 1 on file open failure (lines 91-106)\n     - R4.3: `epipeOr1()` returns 1 for non-EPIPE write errors (lines 257-262); main flush handles write errors (lines 35-40)\n     - Key function signatures: `func main()`, `func parseArgs(args []string) (options, string, string, bool)`, `func run(w *bufio.Writer, opts *options, path1, path2 string) int`, `func compare(w *bufio.Writer, opts *options, r1, r2 io.Reader) int`, `func writeLine(w *bufio.Writer, opts *options, col int, line string) error`, `func epipeOr1(err error) int`\n\n   - `cmd/comm/comm_test.go` (386 lines, existing tests)\n     - Has `TestDiff` with 44 differential test cases covering R1-R3\n     - Has `TestSIGPIPE` (lines 350-378) already testing R4.4\n     - Uses `normStderr` function to normalize program names in stderr output\n     - Helper function `writeFile` for creating test fixtures\n     - Missing: explicit differential test cases for R4.2 (file not found errors)\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. Was in the reading/planning phase.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Identified that R4.1-R4.4 functionality is already implemented in the existing main.go code\n   - The main gap is in test coverage: need differential test cases that explicitly exercise R4.2 (nonexistent file) to verify exit code matches gcomm\n   - R4.1 is implicitly tested by all passing tests but may benefit from explicit naming\n   - R4.3 is difficult to test differentially (can't easily trigger stdout write error in both binaries simultaneously)\n   - R4.4 already has a dedicated TestSIGPIPE test\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - One massive orchestrator-generated task prompt containing: role definition, repository file listing, project context (vision, architecture, specifications, roadmap, analysis, requirement states), execution constitution, go style constitution, task description with requirements/design decisions/acceptance criteria, shared protocols, and package contracts\n   - Second message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - requesting a summary of the conversation\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Add differential test cases for R4.2 (file open errors - nonexistent files) to `cmd/comm/comm_test.go`\n   - Potentially add test cases for R4.3 (write errors) if feasible in differential testing\n   - Verify the implementation handles all edge cases for R4.1-R4.4\n   - Run `go build -o bin/comm ./cmd/comm/` to verify compilation\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/comm/ -count=1` to verify tests pass\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/comm/` to verify no issues\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading all three required files (srd029-comm.yaml, cmd/comm/main.go, cmd/comm/comm_test.go) and was in the planning/analysis phase before implementation. I identified that the core R4.1-R4.4 functionality already exists in main.go, and the main work needed is adding differential test cases (especially for R4.2 - file-not-found scenarios) to comm_test.go to ensure exit codes and stderr output match the gcomm reference binary.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Add differential test cases to `cmd/comm/comm_test.go` for R4.1-R4.4, primarily:\n   - R4.2 test: Pass a nonexistent file path to verify exit code 1 and stderr error message matches gcomm (using `normStderr` normalizer)\n   - Potentially an explicit R4.1 test verifying exit 0 on clean run (already covered implicitly)\n   - Then run `go build -o bin/comm ./cmd/comm/` and `go test ./cmd/comm/ -count=1` and `go vet ./cmd/comm/` to verify acceptance criteria AC1-AC5.\n\n   The task description states: \"Implement srd029-comm R4.1 per the SRD specification\", \"Implement srd029-comm R4.2 per the SRD specification\", \"Implement srd029-comm R4.3 per the SRD specification\", \"Implement srd029-comm R4.4 per the SRD specification\" with acceptance criteria requiring \"All R4.1-R4.4 requirements from srd029-comm are implemented\" and \"Differential tests for R4.1-R4.4 pass against gcomm reference binary\".\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5300/eec2d7d4-6fb8-4ed4-906b-4d708cb11d02.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eec2d7d4-6fb8-4ed4-906b-4d708cb11d02","uuid":"f70456a7-1121-44a7-a47d-e59572b49a2e","timestamp":"2026-05-19T22:05:37.700Z","isSynthetic":true}
